        "content": "The selling price",
        "rationale": "Using the selling price gives a smaller percentage and is not the usual definition."
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "content": "The profit",
        "rationale": "The profit is the amount being expressed as a percentage, not the base."
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "content": "The marked price",
        "rationale": "The marked price is used for discounts, not for profit."
      }
    ],
    "explanation": "Percentage profit (and loss) is calculated on the cost price: $\\frac{\\text{profit}}{\\text{cost price}} \\times 100$.",
